{"type":"text","timestamp":1794256039271,"sessionID":"ses_e3e043f3bffePqMA3HpHvx6uR5","part":{"id":"prt_1c1fe6d4d00184jLR5OUOz1NPj","messageID":"msg_1c1fe5199001XR47O7BG8lyX6v","sessionID":"ses_e3e043f3bffePqMA3HpHvx6uR5","type":"text","text":"The shortener is built, but I haven't run it in Docker or in a browser. The sandbox has no Docker, so I never ran the container build. I didn't test the frontend beyond a successful `npm run build` (type-check plus Vite). I tested the API through Flask's test client. That run covered:\n\n- register and login\n- the admin login\n- creating a link\n- the 302 redirect with the click count\n- the 403 on someone else's link\n- the admin list and toggle\n- a disabled link answering 404 and dropping out of the public list\n- rejection of non-http addresses\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`)\n- The database is SQLite at `data/app.db`.\n- Passwords are hashed.\n- Login tokens are random and last 30 days. They are stored hashed and sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.\n- The admin account exists only when `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is set. Its sign-in is disabled otherwise, and nobody can register the name `admin`.\n- Errors come back as `{\"error\": \"...\"}`, and unknown `/api/...` paths answer a JSON 404.\n- `GET /r/<code>` is its own route, so it takes precedence over the frontend.\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/src`)\n- It uses React with Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`), and `index.css` only imports Tailwind.\n- It has sign-in and register forms, the signed-in username with a sign-out button, and the shorten form with a copy button.\n- The links table shows truncated original addresses with the full value on hover, click counts, dates and paging. Delete asks for confirmation and appears only on your own links.\n- The admin gets a \"Moderation\" tab listing all links with owners and a Disable/Enable button.\n- The session token is kept in `localStorage`.\n\nBeyond the spec:\n- `npm run build` now runs `tsc --noEmit` before Vite.\n- The admin list items carry an extra `active` field so the frontend can show which links are disabled.\n- I added a `.gitignore`.\n\nI added no backend dependencies, so `requirements.txt` and `requirements.lock` are unchanged. The frontend lockfile is updated for the new packages.","time":{"start":1794256039245,"end":1794256039251}}}
